Currently, we have lots of imports and registration stuff we have to handle. Decorations allow us to 'magically' do things which simplyfies some stuff.

This PR also comes with an command method decorator - see the example below.

##### Example
```ts
class MyCommandGroup {
    @command('reviveme', '/reviveme - Revives you.', PERMISSIONS.ADMIN)
    static reviveMe(player: alt.Player) {
        player.health = 200;
        player.clearBloodDamage();
        player.spawn(player.pos);
    }
}
```

##### Another useful decorator would be an interaction decorator made by @Booster1212:
```ts
export function interaction(pos: IVector3, description: string, dim: number) {
    return (_target: Function, _propertyName: string, descriptor: PropertyDescriptor) => {
        const callback: (player: alt.Player, ...args: any[]) => void = descriptor.value;
        Athena.controllers.interaction.add({
            position: pos,
            description: description,
            dimension: dim,
            callback: callback,
        });
    };
}
```

##### Usage
```ts
class MyInteractions {
    @interaction({ x: 0, y: 0, z: 71 }, 'My amazing description', 0)
    static myInteraction(_player: alt.Player) {
        alt.log('Yaay, i got called!');
    }
}
```

